# data-table.ine — tabular data display written with ONLY the current
# dictionary vocabulary (page, header, logo, navigation, container,
# card-group, card, section, button, footer, title/text).
#
# Evidence-collection experiment (PLAN mission 73): a table needs rows,
# columns, headers, and sortable values. This program shows what that
# intent reduces to when the only structural grouping is a card-group of
# cards and the only value a property carries is text.
# Every line the vocabulary could not guide is flagged with `vocab gap:`
# and listed in .agent/NOTES.md ("## Mission 73").

make page
page title "Deployments"

make header
header inside page
make logo
logo text "Acme Ops"
logo inside header
make navigation
navigation inside header

# A table is a set of rows sharing a column shape. The dictionary has no
# table/row/cell kinds, so every row becomes a card and every column a
# text property. Rows only sit inside a card-group inside a container.
make table container
table inside page
make rows card-group
rows inside table
make row-1 card
make row-2 card
make row-3 card
make 4 card
# vocab gap: `make 4 card` after the explicit row cards does NOT collide
# this time (explicit names are on a different batch), but `make N card`
# still restarts at card-1..card-4. Four real rows need eight cards in
# reality; here three explicit rows demonstrate the shape.

group table_rows = row-1 row-2 row-3 card-1 card-2 card-3 card-4
table_rows inside rows
row-1 title "Service | Version | Status | Region"
row-1 text "api | v2.14 | live | us-east-1"
row-2 title "web | v2.1 | live | eu-west-1"
row-2 text "worker | v4.3 | paused | us-east-1"
row-3 title "db | v9.0 | draining | ap-south-1"
# vocab gap: a "table" is column headers crammed into a title string and
# cell values crammed into a text string. There is no column concept, no
# per-cell property, no header row vs. data row, and no alignment: nothing
# about this renders as a grid. The separator (" | ") is a display
# convention living in the source; a cell's value cannot be referenced,
# sorted, or reformatted separately from the whole string.

card-1 title "rank"
card-1 text "1st place"
card-2 title "score"
card-2 text "998"
card-3 title "trend"
card-3 text "up"
card-4 title "notes"
card-4 text "sorted by rank"
# vocab gap: was *supposed* to show a second "sortable data" perspective,
# but a card's only values are its own title/text — there is no way to say
# "sort this column" or "this cell belongs to a column". Sorting intent
# cannot exist because the data is not structurally tabular.

# Sort/action affordance: a table usually has a sort control.
make toolbar section
toolbar title "Table actions"
toolbar inside page
make sort button
sort text "Sort by version"
sort inside toolbar
# vocab gap: the button prints but does nothing — no interaction model
# (mission 74) and no way to associate "sort by version" with a specific
# column.

make footer
footer text "Ine — data-table experiment"
footer inside page

say page title
say row-1 title